On Wed, Mar 6, 2013 at 1:48 AM, la gleki <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com> wrote:
> An old issue but still is there any solution?
> Let's imagine we want to add a fuhivla e.g. {bacriedgo} that camxes parses
> but jbovlaste doesn't want to add (it says "Sorry, that isn't actually a
> word in Lojban. (Did you remember to strip leading and/or trailing
> pauses?)").
> What can be done to override that?

Probably it's best to avoid such words. Presumably jbovlaste will
accept "criedigo" (which camxes doesn't) and that's why it can't
accept "bacriedigo", as at most one of those two forms could be a
Lojban word.

